      "content": "The specific temperature curve depends on the cocoa butter content, but generally, you need to melt the chocolate gently (around 45-50°C). Then, temper it by cooling it down to a specific nucleation temperature (often around 27-29°C). Finally, reheat it slightly back up (around 31-32°C) to encourage the formation of stable, desirable Form V crystals. Adhering strictly to these precise stages guarantees the correct crystal structure to resist future fat bloom.",
